{
  "comment": "Class-level displayTemplate (SCHEMA.md): class.create/class.update carry the OPTIONAL NULLABLE displayTemplate — an optional format string render surfaces apply to the derived titles of the class's members (e.g. \"@{{citekey}}\" for sources). Tri-state, exactly like color: absent = inherit (no write — a re-issued create's COALESCE preserves the stored value), a non-empty string = the template, \"\" = an EXPLICIT opt-out (round-trips as '' and STOPS extends-inheritance for the class and its subclasses), present null = clear back to NULL/inherit. The applier maps it to the class registry column class.display_template (store schema v36) ONLY — unlike parentless_role the node row is NOT a carrier; display reads go through the store helpers (resolveEffectiveDisplayTemplate walks extends-ancestors nearest-first, the first non-NULL ancestor value decides, an ancestor '' stops the walk). This fixture pins the payload shapes: Source seeds the template \"@{{citekey}}\"; a member object.create is the population the template renders over; Book extends Source with no own template (inheritance); Web link extends Source and opts out via class.update {displayTemplate: \"\"} (the ancestor's template is still live at that point — the own '' must win); finally Source's template is CLEARED by a present-null class.update (back to NULL/inherit).",
